This is a copy of github.com/masahiro331/go-ext4-filesystem at
v0.0.0-20260423010602-fe51f5b5e52b (Apache License 2.0, see LICENSE),
used by BackupZit through a replace directive in its go.mod.

Changes by BackupZit (2026-11-19):
- ext4/inode.go: Extent.IsUninitialized and Extent.GetLen follow the
  Linux kernel (ext4_ext_is_unwritten, ext4_ext_get_actual_len): an
  extent of length 0x8000 is an initialized extent of 32768 blocks, not
  an unwritten one. Before, files restored from ext4 returned zeros for
  every such extent (most files above 128 MiB). Reported with a fix by
  gtawelt (BackupZit PR #49; upstream masahiro331/go-ext4-filesystem#24).
- ext4/fs.go (2026-11-20): Open follows at most 40 symbolic links (a link to
  itself recursed until the stack overflowed), reads a link by its full
  path, and resolves a relative target in the link's folder.
- ext4/fs.go, ext4/ext4.go (2026-11-20): NewFS refuses an implausible
  superblock (block size above 64 KiB, zero blocks or inodes per group,
  more groups than the volume holds); the extent tree walk stops after as
  many nodes and extents as the volume has blocks (at most 4 Mi).
- The upstream tests are left out.

Drop this copy once upstream has the fix.
